L(308, 308, "  - **Giving no further word is the owner's choice,", '''
  - **Giving no further word.** Every generation needs its own word (D22), so no rule here can compel one. But a withheld word concludes nothing. The pilot stays pending, the floor has no value, and no production cell registers: production does not start on a CHORUS-only floor because a word was withheld. v5 let the owner record that no further word would come, which concluded the pilot with no value. After a rejected AI_READI attempt, with whatever its saved stages show, its coverage readings included, that could keep the floor at CHORUS's known value by giving up AI_READI. **Taking AI_READI out of scope after a rejected attempt, without its second attempt, now takes a ratified change to this amendment.** Under NP1.5 such a change applies only to cells registered after it and defines a new prospective stratum, whose pilot requirements are fixed before any pilot in it. The same holds for the replacement pilot and for the canary: with no further word each stays pending.
''')
